WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.580
A quiet room.

2
00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.380
Nobody else is home.

3
00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.290
Then, a voice.

4
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.270
As clear as anyone's.

5
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.970
But there's no one there.

6
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:13.920
So what is the brain doing, when someone
hears a voice and no one is there?

7
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:18.410
In this mission, you'll learn that
hearing voices can be a hallucination:

8
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.400
a symptom of schizophrenia,
a severe mental illness.

9
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.380
You'll zoom in on how neurons
pass signals across synapses,

10
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.830
using chemical messengers
called neurotransmitters.

11
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.670
And you'll see how different areas
of the brain do different jobs,

12
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.390
such as handling sound and language.

13
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.770
Your mission: find out what the brain
is doing when someone hears a voice that

14
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.720
isn't there.
